    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατόχ-ῐμος</span></b> , later form for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατοκώχιμος</span> (q. v.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>held in possession</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς αἰῶνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Le.</u>
					25.46
				</span></i>
			; <i>sequestered</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλῆρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PFrankf.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				9
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				61
			</span></i> (<i>b</i>).<i><span class="en">
				253
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>possessed</i> by a supernatural power, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατοκώχιμον</span>
			, <u>Gloss.</u>; of things, '<i>eerie', uncanny</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. πάντα καὶ φρικώδη καὶ μυστικά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>JTr.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			. </div>
